mpts":null,"reflection_prompt":null,"teach_steps":[{"icon":"🔎","title":"Use addition bonds","explain":"**Why this works:** 20−8=12 because 8+12=20.\n\n**Remember:** Use the original facts, numbers and positions rather than guessing. This lesson investigates subtraction fluency: facts with reasons.","example":"**MY THINKING:** 20−8=12 because 8+12=20.\n\n**YOUR TRY:** Solve 19−7, 30−16, 51−27, 90−38, 124−58 and 201−96. Show strategies for at least four and explain how you checked two.\n\n**CHECK:** Read the model and explain where each number or supporting detail came from.","notice":"20−8=12 because 8+12=20. Keep your work accurate and name the strategy.","check":{"question":"20−8?","options":["10","11","12","13"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The correct choice is 12. 20−8=12 because 8+12=20."},"visual_before":[{"episode":{"title":"Investigate Subtraction Fluency: Facts with Reasons","transcript":"Pip: I found a tricky task and need a reliable method.\nJuno: Look carefully at the example and explain each step.\nPip: I can use the worked example to check my answer.\nJuno: Pause and try solving one part before the next stage.","scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"who":"pip","text":"I found a tricky task and need a reliable method. How do I decide what to do?"},{"who":"juno","text":"This is subtraction fluency: facts with reasons. Look carefully at the example and explain each step."},{"who":"pip","text":"I can use the worked example to check my answer and explain my method."},{"who":"juno","text":"Pause and try solving one part before the next stage. Check it carefully, including the original numbers or supporting words.","pause_after":true}]}]}}]},{"icon":"📚","title":"Subtract a friendly multiple of ten","explain":"**Why this works:** 35−17=35−20+3=18.\n\n**Remember:** Use the original facts, numbers and positions rather than guessing. This lesson investigates subtraction fluency: facts with reasons.","example":"**MY THINKING:** 35−17=35−20+3=18.\n\n**YOUR TRY:** Solve 19−7, 30−16, 51−27, 90−38, 124−58 and 201−96. Show strategies for at least four and explain how you checked two.\n\n**CHECK:** Read the model and explain where each number or supporting detail came from.","notice":"35−17=35−20+3=18. Keep your work accurate and name the strategy.","check":{"question":"35−17?","options":["17","18","19","22"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is 18. 35−17=35−20+3=18."}},{"icon":"✏️","title":"Partition larger differences","explain":"**Why this works:** 80−46=80−40−6=34.\n\n**Remember:** Use the original facts, numbers and positions rather than guessing. This lesson investigates subtraction fluency: facts with reasons.","example":"**MY THINKING:** 80−46=80−40−6=34.\n\n**YOUR TRY:** Solve 19−7, 30−16, 51−27, 90−38, 124−58 and 201−96. Show strategies for at least four and explain how you checked two.\n\n**CHECK:** Read the model and explain where each number or supporting detail came from.","notice":"80−46=80−40−6=34. Keep your work accurate and name the strategy.","check":{"question":"80−46?","options":["24","34","44","36"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is 34. 80−46=80−40−6=34."}},{"icon":"✅","title":"Use addition to verify","explain":"**Why this works:** 104−59=104−60+1=45; 45+59=104.\n\n**Remember:** Use the original facts, numbers and positions rather than guessing. This lesson investigates subtraction fluency: facts with reasons.","example":"**MY THINKING:** 104−59=104−60+1=45; 45+59=104.\n\n**YOUR TRY:** Solve 19−7, 30−16, 51−27, 90−38, 124−58 and 201−96. Show strategies for at least four and explain how you checked two.\n\n**CHECK:** Read the model and explain where each number or supporting detail came from.","notice":"104−59=104−60+1=45; 45+59=104. Keep your work accurate and name the strategy.","check":{"question":"104−59?","options":["35","45","55","65"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"The correct choice is 45. 104−59=104−60+1=45; 45+59=104."}}],"worked_example":"A Year 3 class is checking the answers to several subtraction problems using different methods.\n\n1. Use addition bonds: 20−8=12 because 8+12=20.\n\n2. Subtract a friendly multiple of ten: 35−17=35−20+3=18.\n\n3. Partition larger differences: 80−46=80−40−6=34.\n\n4. Use addition to verify: 104−59=104−60+1=45; 45+59=104.\n\nCheck how the final answer follows from the original information.","worked_visuals":[{"svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 590 180\"><rect width=\"590\" height=\"180\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f6f9f7\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"28\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"18\">Learn, practise and check</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"60\" width=\"135\" height=\"95\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e0eee4\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"100\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"13\">STEP ONE</text><rect x=\"151\" y=\"60\" width=\"135\" height=\"95\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8eefa\"/><text x=\"159\" y=\"100\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"13\">STEP TWO</text><rect x=\"294\" y=\"60\" width=\"135\" height=\"95\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e0eee4\"/><text x=\"302\" y=\"100\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"13\">STEP THREE</text><rect x=\"437\" y=\"60\" width=\"135\" height=\"95\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8eefa\"/><text x=\"445\" y=\"100\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"13\">STEP FOUR</text></svg>","alt":"Four-stage reminder for Subtraction Fluency: Facts with Reasons.","caption":"Use this to keep track of the four teaching ideas."}],"guided_practice":"**First follow the model:** 20−8=12 because 8+12=20. 35−17=35−20+3=18. 80−46=80−40−6=34. 104−59=104−60+1=45; 45+59=104.\n\n**Now attempt a new challenge before checking the answer:** Solve 19−7, 30−16, 51−27, 90−38, 124−58 and 201−96. Show strategies for at least four and explain how you checked two.\n\n**Feedback:** The answers are 12, 14, 24, 52, 66 and 105 respectively. One strategy: 90−38=90−40+2=52.\n\n**Important correction:** 90−38 is 52, not 62. 52+38=90 confirms the subtraction. Invent a fact family: 52+38=90 and 90−38=52.","independent_task":"Solve 19−7, 30−16, 51−27, 90−38, 124−58 and 201−96. Show strategies for at least four and explain how you checked two.","response_prompt":"Solve 19−7, 30−16, 51−27, 90−38, 124−58 and 201−96. Show strategies for at least four and explain how you checked two.","quiz":[{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"20−8?","options":["10","11","12","13"],"correct_index":2,"explanation":"12 is supported by the original worked examples."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"35−17?","options":["17","18","19","22"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"18 is supported by the original worked examples."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"80−46?","options":["24","34","44","36"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"34 is supported by the original worked examples."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"104−59?","options":["35","45","55","65"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"45 is supported by the original worked examples."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"42−19?","options":["22","23","24","33"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"23 is supported by the original worked examples."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"73−28?","options":["35","45","55","46"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"45 is supported by the original worked examples."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"100−64?","options":["26","36","46","56"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"36 is supported by the original worked examples."},{"type":"multiple_choice","question":"90−38?","options":["42","52","62","58"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"52 is supported by the original worked examples."},{"type":"short_answer","question":"Complete the challenge, showing the supporting information or calculations.","sample_answer":"The answers are 12, 14, 24, 52, 66 and 105 respectively. One strategy: 90−38=90−40+2=52.","marking_guide":"Check all requested components against the supplied worked method.","explanation":"An answer needs accurate steps, not only a final number."},{"type":"short_answer","question":"Describe and correct a specific possible misconception.","sample_answer":"90−38 is 52, not 62. 52+38=90 confirms the subtraction. Invent a fact family: 52+38=90 and 90−38=52.","marking_guide":"Require a relevant check and accurate correction.","explanation":"An explanation shows understanding."}],"parent_notes":"Parent: Check the child''s independent strategy or text evidence and ask them to explain one detail without copying.\n\nParent: Written model one: The answers are 12, 14, 24, 52, 66 and 105 respectively. One strategy: 90−38=90−40+2=52.\n\nParent: Written model two: 90−38 is 52, not 62. 52+38=90 confirms the subtraction. Invent a fact family: 52+38=90 and 90−38=52.\n\nParent: Save original evidence, manually check written work and verify syllabus alignment separately.","evidence_instructions":"Keep the guided practice, original task, one corrected error and the two written quiz responses.","offline_alternative":"Use paper and a pencil for the teaching and independent problem. A parent may record oral explanations.","extension":"Create an additional subtraction fluency: facts with reasons problem and justify its solution.","stage_hints":{"accept":["Read the instruction and find the relevant information for Subtraction Fluency: Facts with Reasons.","Think about how the worked example makes each step clear.","Check a specific number or clue, then explain your own answer."],"teach0":["Read the instruction and find the relevant information for Use addition bonds.","Think about how the worked example makes each step clear.","Check a specific number or clue, then explain your own answer."],"teach1":["Read the instruction and find the relevant information for Subtract a friendly multiple of ten.","Think about how the worked example makes each step clear.","Check a specific number or clue, then explain your own answer."],"teach2":["Read the instruction and find the relevant information for Partition larger differences.","Think about how the worked example makes each step clear.","Check a specific number 